WEBVTT

00:07:59.448 --> 00:08:03.497
It's a way of using the language between actual people.

00:08:03.497 --> 00:08:06.736
Another example is "slash."

00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:09.504
Now, we can use slash in the way that we're used to,

00:08:09.504 --> 00:08:11.144
along the lines of, "We're going to have

00:08:11.144 --> 00:08:14.626
a party-slash-networking session."

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:16.720
That's kind of like what we're at.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.259
Slash is used in a very different way

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:23.217
in texting among young people today.

00:08:23.217 --> 00:08:25.070
It's used to change the scene.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.019
So for example, this Sally person says,

00:08:28.019 --> 00:08:29.824
"So I need to find people to chill with"

00:08:29.824 --> 00:08:31.343
and Jake says, "Haha" --